<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sacramento Valley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sacramento Valley is the northern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>'s Central Valley, drained by the Sacramento River. In the 1840s American settlers gathered there around Sutter's Fort, and in June 1846 a group of them began the Bear Flag Revolt against Mexican rule. The discovery of gold at Sutter's Mill in 1848 nearby started the California Gold Rush.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sacramento-valley.jpg" alt="Sacramento Valley" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DevinCook at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sacramento_Riverfront.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
